<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.7.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00485</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.7.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9983b6b2-8c74-4a2c-b5df-900bd0efa8c4</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice">
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <para>For questions 1 – 8, solve each system of equations to determine if there is one
        solution, no solution, or infinitely many solutions.</para>

        <exercise id="_2a17b9ee-0868-435e-9a4f-0dbdd1d9ec7c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>
              \(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}5x\;-\;3y\;&amp;=&amp;\;7\\x\;-\;0.6y\;&amp;=&amp;\;1.4\end{array}\right.\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! infinitely many solutions</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.7.1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is infinitely many solutions.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_664076ff-bb5c-445e-8be2-859452344a5f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>
              \(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}-x\;+\;2y\;&amp;=&amp;\;-1\\5x\;-\;10y\;&amp;=&amp;\;6\end{array}\right.\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! no solution</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.7.2 .</para>
            <para>The correct answer is no solutions.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="e49b74e7-9d0c-459f-bfe4-246f55d48cbe" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>
              \(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}7x+6y&amp;=&amp;2\\-28x-24y&amp;=&amp;-8\end{array}\right.\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! infinitely many solutions</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.7.1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is infinitely many solutions.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_71d06919-7e8f-4cb4-88f2-64dfc9b5aa60" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>
              \(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}-0.2x\;+\;0.4y\;&amp;=&amp;\;0.6\\x-2y&amp;=&amp;-3\end{array}\right.\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! infinitely many solutions</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.7.1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is infinitely many solutions.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_4db03d63-ee9f-4b64-94af-63c24270bc96" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>
              \(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}-0.1x\;+\;0.2y\;&amp;=&amp;\;0.6\\5x-10y&amp;=&amp;1\end{array}\right.\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! no solution</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.7.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is infinitely no solution.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_750540c7-d146-4947-8f4d-311f1f65f541" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>
              \(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}3x+6y&amp;=&amp;11\\\;2x+4y&amp;=&amp;9\end{array}\right.\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! no solution</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.7.2 .</para>
            <para>The correct answer is no solution.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="c4feb987-f0b2-46ca-8d87-dda6dbc51f6f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}-x+2y=4\\\;2x-4y&amp;=&amp;1\end{array}\right.\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! no solution</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.7.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is no solution.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="c5397197-3143-4960-9059-4af843fb916d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>
              \(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}3x-2y&amp;=&amp;5\\\;-9x+6y&amp;=&amp;-15\end{array}\right.\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! infinitely many solutions</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.7.1 .</para>
            <para>The correct answer is infinitely many solutions.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_96189aa5-1253-411f-9357-e39b90990101" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which system of equations has infinitely many solutions?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}4x\;+\;3y\;=\;12\\8x\;+\;6y\;=\;-24\end{array}\right.\)</para>
            <para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}4x\;+\;3y\;=\;12\\8x\;+\;6y\;=\;12\end{array}\right.\)</para>
            <para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}-4x\;+\;3y\;=\;12\\8x\;-\;6y\;=\;\;24\end{array}\right.\)</para>
            <para>
              \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}-4x\;+\;3y\;=\;-12\\-8x\;+\;6y\;=\;-24\end{array}\right.\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(-4x + 3y = -12\) and \(-8x + 6y = -24\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.7.3 and 2.7.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(-4x + 3y = -12\) and \(-8x + 6y = -24\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_64f15677-6ec4-4a06-b000-22081ca23b7c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Multiple choice:</para>
            <para>Which system of equations has no solution?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}3x+7y=15\\3x+7y=40\end{array}\right.\)</para>
            <para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}3x+7y=15\\6x+14y=30\end{array}\right.\)</para>
            <para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}3x-7y=15\\3x+7y=40\end{array}\right.\)</para>
            <para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}9x+21y=270\\3x+7y=90\end{array}\right.\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(3x + 7y = 15\) and \(3x + 7y = 40\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.7.3 and 2.7.4 .</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(3x + 7y = 15\) and \(3x + 7y = 40\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
<section><exercise id="_2a17b9ee-0868-435e-9a4f-0dbdd1d9ec7c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}5x\;-\;3y\;&amp;=&amp;\;7\\x\;-\;0.6y\;&amp;=&amp;\;1.4\end{array}\right.\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! infinitely many solutions</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.7.1.</para><para>The correct answer is infinitely many solutions.</para></solution></exercise>
      
