      </problem><solution><para>Correct! infinitely many solutions</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.7.1.</para><para>The correct answer is infinitely many solutions.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_4db03d63-ee9f-4b64-94af-63c24270bc96" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}-0.1x\;+\;0.2y\;&amp;=&amp;\;0.6\\5x-10y&amp;=&amp;1\end{array}\right.\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! no solution</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.7.2.</para><para>The correct answer is infinitely no solution.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_750540c7-d146-4947-8f4d-311f1f65f541" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}3x+6y&amp;=&amp;11\\\;2x+4y&amp;=&amp;9\end{array}\right.\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! no solution</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.7.2 .</para><para>The correct answer is no solution.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="c4feb987-f0b2-46ca-8d87-dda6dbc51f6f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}-x+2y=4\\\;2x-4y&amp;=&amp;1\end{array}\right.\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! no solution</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.7.2.</para><para>The correct answer is no solution.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="c5397197-3143-4960-9059-4af843fb916d" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}3x-2y&amp;=&amp;5\\\;-9x+6y&amp;=&amp;-15\end{array}\right.\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! infinitely many solutions</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.7.1 .</para><para>The correct answer is infinitely many solutions.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_96189aa5-1253-411f-9357-e39b90990101" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which system of equations has infinitely many solutions?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}4x\;+\;3y\;=\;12\\8x\;+\;6y\;=\;-24\end{array}\right.\)</para><para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}4x\;+\;3y\;=\;12\\8x\;+\;6y\;=\;12\end{array}\right.\)</para><para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}-4x\;+\;3y\;=\;12\\8x\;-\;6y\;=\;\;24\end{array}\right.\)</para><para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}-4x\;+\;3y\;=\;-12\\-8x\;+\;6y\;=\;-24\end{array}\right.\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(-4x + 3y = -12\) and \(-8x + 6y = -24\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.7.3 and 2.7.4.</para><para>The correct answer is \(-4x + 3y = -12\) and \(-8x + 6y = -24\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_64f15677-6ec4-4a06-b000-22081ca23b7c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Multiple choice:</para><para>Which system of equations has no solution?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}3x+7y=15\\3x+7y=40\end{array}\right.\)</para><para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}3x+7y=15\\6x+14y=30\end{array}\right.\)</para><para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}3x-7y=15\\3x+7y=40\end{array}\right.\)</para><para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}9x+21y=270\\3x+7y=90\end{array}\right.\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(3x + 7y = 15\) and \(3x + 7y = 40\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.7.3 and 2.7.4 .</para><para>The correct answer is \(3x + 7y = 15\) and \(3x + 7y = 40\).</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
